From f60f950eea82fb957bf0deb62da59686d6513356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:39:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1011/1178] Writing room from YuE2 Studio, lyrics check by
 Whisper, bracket rule fixed

HERESY 1011.
- Writing room (heresy-assist.js): YuE2 Studio's songwriting assistant
  (Apache-2.0), its songwriter.md verbatim and its assist(): five tasks
  (song, lyrics, style, review, adapt), the current title, style, lyrics and
  score as context, the user's standing writing preferences, a JSON draft with
  notes that are never sung, apply all / lyrics / style and one undo. One rule
  added and measured: style against the score (key, meter, tempo must agree;
  a contradicting style lost 0.14 of lyric recognition over two seeds).
  chatComplete takes an optional temperature; null lets the server choose.
- Lyrics check in the take card (heresy-gloss.js): Whisper large-v3 on Forge
  through /lab (loaded per take, VRAM freed after), matched to the lyrics per
  minute: coloured minute bars, furthest line reached, returns back, every
  heard segment with its closest lyric line; a click plays from there. A
  Whisper loop on one text is flagged as a void measurement.
- The bracket rule of 1009 was wrong: 29 of the 110 official examples have
  lines in brackets, instrument cues like (saxophone) among them. Only the
  shapes none has are flagged now: a "Label:", an arrow or a p/f mark inside.
- Folded Prompt and Lyrics headings no longer wrap under their peek.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
